== What this feature implements ==

1. `apps/api/src/application/asset/write-asset-visibility.ts` (new): the single function that
   persists a visibility-bearing `AssetGovernanceRecord` (`writeAssetGovernanceVisibility`) and
   derives `requiresCosign` from it. This is the one and only call site of
   `AssetGovernanceRepository.set` for a governance write anywhere under
   `apps/api/src/{application,domain}/asset` -- enforced by a source-scan test
   (`visibility-single-write-path.test.ts`) so a future automatic downgrade (`uc-23-6`,
   F138/F139, not built here) has structurally nowhere else to write from (domain I-14).

2. `apps/api/src/application/asset/set-asset-governance.ts` (modified): now delegates the
   actual persistence + `requiresCosign` derivation to `writeAssetGovernanceVisibility` instead
   of calling `deps.governance.set` inline. Permission/completeness checks (already F134's
   scope) are unchanged.

3. `visibility-whole-org-requires-cosign.test.ts` (new): `visibility: "whole-org"` ->
   `requiresCosign: true` (with counter-proof against always-true/always-false); `visibility:
   "specified-teams"` with empty `teamIds` cannot be saved (`GOVERNANCE_INCOMPLETE`, folded into
   the `visibility` field per F134's own design, not a fifth field); and the response shape
   carries no invented approval-flow field (only `governance` + `requiresCosign`).

4. `visibility-single-write-path.test.ts` (new): source-scans `src/application/asset` and
   `src/domain/asset` to assert exactly one call site of `governance.set(...)` exists (in
   `write-asset-visibility.ts`), plus a behavioral check that `setAssetGovernance`'s persisted
   side effect is identical to calling `writeAssetGovernanceVisibility` directly.

Not implemented (out of scope, matches issue #252's own boundary notes):
- The cosign/联签 approval workflow itself ([待确认], `uc-23-4` A1) -- only `requiresCosign: true`
  is surfaced, no approval state machine invented.
- The automatic 30-day-no-review downgrade (`uc-23-6`, F138/F139) -- this feature only makes
  the write path a future downgrade must use, it does not build the scan/timer/downgrade logic.
- Enforcing `负责人 ∈ editableBy` (Q-9, undecided).
